From 7ae173a6576a7e795eddab67009f9b0517b3b403 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Payton <brandon@happycode.net>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:31:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] Go: Implement homogeneous wasm32 cgo calls and
 callbacks

Use ordinary typed C pointer fields and export frames with four-byte Go
pointers. Adapt the Kandelo C-call, bootstrap and callback ABI0 assembly,
preserving both logical PCs and table handles across foreign callbacks.
Remove the unused mixed-width Kandelo assembly from this prototype.

Parse Wasm objects and passive data in cgo's import scan, rejecting unknown
import namespaces rather than inventing dynamic-library bindings. Passive
bytes do not become initialized addressable constants. Keep upstream cgo
argument/export layouts and pointer types unchanged.

Resolve C function addresses as table handles. Record the exact C frame
signature so asmcgocall handles void wrappers and errno-returning wrappers
without an indirect-call type mismatch. Stop rooting references inside
unused C functions; normal linker reachability must select those callees.
Register cgo support and keep the existing VFS account lookup in both modes.

Validation: five standard-library builds; host cgo/object-reader/platform
tests; WASI wasm32/wasm runtime controls; seven Node cases and 21 browser
cases across Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. Exercise typed struct fields,
escaping field-address GC roots, by-value aggregates, C function pointers,
errno, per-M TLS, callbacks, C-created pthread stack growth and callback/GC
churn. Full Go/cgo conformance and application migration remain pending.

